The rule for recover_json_object says the object scored is the last one inside a code fence when any fence holds one, else the last top-level object in the text. For the input fence[ A B ] A, the fence holds A and B, so the last object inside the fence is B, and recovery should return B. For the rewritten text fence[ A B ] A A, the fence still holds A and B, so the last object inside the fence remains B, and recovery should still return B. Therefore the recovery answer is unchanged between the two texts.